<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Appraisal readiness checkup</span><i>12 questions · about two minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get the carrier’s coverage position in writing. If the claim was denied outright, talk to an Indiana attorney before considering appraisal."><span>Has the insurer accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask in writing for the full itemized estimate, not just the summary page."><span>Do you have the carrier’s complete line-item estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get a line-item estimate from a contractor or estimator. A one-line bid won’t carry weight with a panel."><span>Do you have your own itemized estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Collect every photo and note its date. Add new photos of current conditions."><span>Do you have dated photos taken soon after the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Locate the ‘Appraisal’ paragraph in the policy conditions and note any deadlines it sets."><span>Have you found and read the appraisal clause in your policy?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Suit Against Us’ condition and put the date on your calendar with our timeline builder."><span>Do you know your policy’s suit-limitation date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make reasonable temporary repairs, such as tarps or water extraction, and keep every receipt."><span>Have temporary repairs been made, with receipts saved?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download or request your declarations page from your agent or carrier."><span>Do you have a current declarations page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure attics, wet walls and roof decking have been checked so the scope is complete."><span>Has hidden damage been opened up and documented?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Gather emails, letters and claim notes in date order."><span>Is your claim correspondence organized by date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run the numbers in our claim gap estimator. A small gap may not justify appraisal costs."><span>Is the gap between estimates more than about 10% or $5,000?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="If a proof of loss was requested, return it on time."><span>If the carrier requested a sworn proof of loss, has it been submitted?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-reset>Reset answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out tool-out-gauge" aria-live="polite">
      <div>
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path class="gauge-track" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Your to-do list</p>
        <ul class="todo" data-o="todo"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="hint">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>How answers are weighted</h2>
<p>Coverage, estimates and evidence carry the most weight because they decide whether appraisal is the right tool and how well your number will hold up. Paperwork items still matter, but they are easier to fix.</p>
<h2>Reading your score</h2>
<ul><li><strong>75 or higher:</strong> the file is in good shape. A professional review of the gap is the sensible next step.</li>
<li><strong>45 to 74:</strong> close the open items first. Each one strengthens your position.</li>
<li><strong>Below 45:</strong> demanding appraisal now could lock in a low number. Build the file first.</li></ul>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Are my answers saved anywhere?</summary><div class="a"><p>No. The checkup runs entirely in your browser and nothing is stored or sent.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I share the result with an appraiser?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. Take a screenshot of your score and to-do list and bring it to your consultation.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free tools</h2><div class="related"><a href="/claim-gap-tools/roof-snow-load-estimator/"><small>Estimator</small><span>Roof Snow Load Estimator</span></a><a href="/claim-gap-tools/claim-gap-net-recovery-estimator/"><small>Estimator</small><span>Claim Gap &amp; Net Recovery Estimator</span></a><a href="/claim-gap-tools/rcv-acv-holdback-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>RCV/ACV Holdback Calculator</span></a></div></article><aside class="sidebar"><div class="sticky"><div class="side-box call-box"><p class="side-h">Talk it through</p><p>A free first conversation. We’ll tell you honestly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="call-num" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-gold btn-block" href="/contact-us/">Send claim details</a></div><div class="side-box"><p class="side-h">All claim tools</p><ul class="side-list"><li><a href="/claim-gap-tools/claim-gap-net-recovery-estimator/">Claim Gap &amp; Net Recovery Estimator</a></li><li><a href="/claim-gap-tools/rcv-acv-holdback-calculator/">RCV/ACV Holdback Calculator</a></li><li><a href="/claim-gap-tools/roof-pitch-squares-calculator/">Roof Pitch &amp; Squares Calculator</a></li><li><a href="/claim-gap-tools/percentage-deductible-calculator/">Percentage Deductible Calculator</a></li><li><a href="/claim-gap-tools/claim-timeline-builder/">Claim Timeline Builder</a></li><li><a href="/claim-gap-tools/appraisal-readiness-checkup/" aria-current="page">Appraisal Readiness Checkup</a></li><li><a href="/claim-gap-tools/roof-snow-load-estimator/">Roof Snow Load Estimator